📌 Polynomial Multiplication (Linked List) — Pseudocode
Assumptions:

  Polynomials are stored in decreasing order of exponent

  No duplicate exponents in a single list

  No term with coefficient = 0
logic :
Input: P1, P2 (head pointers of two polynomial linked lists)
Output: Result (head pointer of multiplied polynomial)

1. If P1 is NULL or P2 is NULL
       return NULL

2. Create Result = NULL

3. Set pointer p = P1

4. While p is not NULL do

       Set pointer q = P2

       While q is not NULL do

            new_coefficient = p.coefficient * q.coefficient
            new_exponent    = p.exponent + q.exponent

            InsertTerm(Result, new_coefficient, new_exponent)

            q = q.next

       End While

       p = p.next

   End While

5. Return Result

1. If coeff == 0
       return

2. If Result is NULL
       create new node and make it head
       return

3. Traverse Result to find position where:
       exponent matches exp
       OR
       correct sorted position

4. If exponent already exists
       add coeff to existing node
       If coefficient becomes 0
              delete that node

5. Else
       insert new node at proper position (maintain decreasing order)

